# SQLite Public Domain Status

The official SQLite source code (https://www.sqlite.org/) is dedicated to the
public domain. From the SQLite website's legal notice:

  All of the code and documentation in SQLite has been dedicated to the
  public domain by its authors. ... The authors disclaim copyright.

The Deno runtime embeds SQLite (via rusty_sqlite / the node:sqlite built-in);
the copy embedded in the `vouch` and `vouch-worker` binaries ships under that
same public-domain dedication. No additional restriction applies.

Retrieved 2026-09-30 from https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html — verify
there before redistribution if this notice ever disagrees with the upstream
page.
